<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Jamf Api on nonpunctual</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/tags/jamf-api/</link><description>Recent content in Jamf Api on nonpunctual</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 21 Dec 2023 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.nonpunctual.org/tags/jamf-api/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Yule Logging</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/yule-logging/</link><pubDate>Thu, 21 Dec 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/yule-logging/</guid><description>&lt;div class="notice info"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Info&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;These posts are being re-created from old Jamf Nation posts not because they are the best but because they may have useful things that were mangled in the &lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/community/jamf-nation/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Nation&lt;/a&gt; transition to its most recent hosting platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That, &amp;amp; they were always supposed to be blog posts anyway&amp;hellip; I didn&amp;rsquo;t have a blog then.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="update-20260822"&gt;&#10; Update (20260822)&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#update-20260822"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In an effort to make this &amp;ldquo;&lt;strong&gt;The Best Logging Thing Available On a Mac&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;rdquo;&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Apple CIDR</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/apple-cidr/</link><pubDate>Mon, 21 Aug 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/apple-cidr/</guid><description>&lt;div class="notice info"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Info&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;These posts are being re-created from old Jamf Nation posts not because they are the best but because they may have useful things that were mangled in the &lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/community/jamf-nation/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Nation&lt;/a&gt; transition to its most recent hosting platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That, &amp;amp; they were always supposed to be blog posts anyway&amp;hellip; I didn&amp;rsquo;t have a blog then.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s been a while so here is something that you may never need, or, you have something clever that you already use for this &amp;amp; I am too dumb to know about it, or, maybe, someone will find it useful.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Dynamic Token Of Static Appreciation</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/dynamic-token-of-static-appreciation/</link><pubDate>Mon, 08 May 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/dynamic-token-of-static-appreciation/</guid><description>&lt;div class="notice info"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Info&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE:&lt;/strong&gt; These posts are being re-created from old Jamf Nation posts not because they are the best but because they may have useful things that were mangled in the &lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/community/jamf-nation/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Nation&lt;/a&gt; transition to its most recent hosting platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That, &amp;amp; they were always supposed to be blog posts anyway&amp;hellip; I didn&amp;rsquo;t have a blog then.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s been a while since I posted anything, so, for (future) me &amp;amp; for you I am posting this script that dynamically updates Static Group membership.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Super Size Me</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/super-size-me/</link><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jun 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/super-size-me/</guid><description>&lt;div class="notice info"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Info&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE:&lt;/strong&gt; These posts are being re-created from old Jamf Nation posts not because they are the best but because they may have useful things that were mangled in the &lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/community/jamf-nation/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Nation&lt;/a&gt; transition to its most recent hosting platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That, &amp;amp; they were always supposed to be blog posts anyway&amp;hellip; I didn&amp;rsquo;t have a blog then.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A while back I posted very excitedly about &lt;a href="https://community.jamf.com/t5/jamf-pro/gnu-new-du-binary-option-in-macos-12-monterey/td-p/252266" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;an update to the &lt;code&gt;du&lt;/code&gt; binary&lt;/a&gt;. I forgot to post that I actually used it for something&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>A Light Unto My Xpath</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/a-light-unto-my-xpath/</link><pubDate>Wed, 22 Dec 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/a-light-unto-my-xpath/</guid><description>&lt;div class="notice info"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Info&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE:&lt;/strong&gt; These posts are being re-created from old Jamf Nation posts not because they are the best but because they may have useful things that were mangled in the &lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/community/jamf-nation/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Nation&lt;/a&gt; transition to its most recent hosting platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That, &amp;amp; they were always supposed to be blog posts anyway&amp;hellip; I didn&amp;rsquo;t have a blog then.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="notice note"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-sticky-note" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Note&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;From the legendary &lt;a href="https://scriptingosx.com/about/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Armin Briegel&lt;/a&gt; in the comments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There seems to be a change to the &lt;code&gt;xmllint&lt;/code&gt; command behavior in Ventura. Now this:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;echo $xml | xmllint --xpath &amp;#39;/policies/policy/id/text()&amp;#39; -&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;returns a new line separated list of all the ids.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Hi Armin -&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It looks like the &lt;code&gt;xmllint&lt;/code&gt; version in macOS has indeed been updated:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;macOS Monterey:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;% sw_vers -productVersion 12.6.2 % xmllint --version xmllint: using libxml version &lt;span style="color:#b48ead"&gt;20904&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;macOS Ventura:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;% sw_vers -productVersion 13.1 % xmllint --version xmllint: using libxml version &lt;span style="color:#b48ead"&gt;20913&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The function for getting ids above still works the same (just tried it on Ventura).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But now it&amp;rsquo;s unnecessary on macOS 13 &amp;amp; later because &lt;code&gt;xmllint&lt;/code&gt; is no longer dumb about output &amp;amp; handles the counting + looping + concatenating behavior for you. This is a good thing!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So, for Monterey &amp;amp; prior (or in Ventura if you don&amp;rsquo;t feel like changing anything&amp;hellip;):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;apiuser&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#39;someuser&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;apipswd&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#39;password&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;jamfurl&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#39;https://somejamfurl.whatever:8443/JSSResource&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;jamfids&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; apidata&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;curl -LSs -X GET -H &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#39;accept: application/xml&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; -u &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;$apiuser&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;$apipswd&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;$jamfurl&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;$1&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; arrsize&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;$apidata&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#eceff4"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; xmllint --xpath &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;//size/text()&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; -&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;i&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;0&lt;span style="color:#eceff4"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;i&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;$arrsize&lt;span style="color:#eceff4"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;i++&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;$apidata&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#eceff4"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; xmllint --xpath &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;concat(//&lt;/span&gt;$2&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;$i&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;]/id/text(),&amp;#39; &amp;#39;)&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; - &lt;span style="color:#eceff4"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;policy_ids&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;jamfids policies policy&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;configuration_profile_ids&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;=(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;jamfids osxconfigurationprofiles os_x_configuration_profile&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1;font-weight:bold"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For Ventura &amp;amp; beyond I still like the idea of a (simplified) generalized function for getting object ids:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;jamfids&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; curl -LSs -X GET -H &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#39;accept: application/xml&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; -u &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;$apiuser&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;$apipswd&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;$jamfurl&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;$1&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#eceff4"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; xmllint --xpath &lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;&amp;#34;//&lt;/span&gt;$2&lt;span style="color:#a3be8c"&gt;/id/text()&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; - &#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#81a1c1"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Thanks!&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember That Time You Wanted All Of Your Self Service Display Names To Actually Match Your Policy Names?</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/self-service-display-names/</link><pubDate>Wed, 24 Jul 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/self-service-display-names/</guid><description>&lt;div class="notice info"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Info&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;These posts are being re-created from old Jamf Nation posts not because they are the best but because they may have useful things that were mangled in the &lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/community/jamf-nation/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Nation&lt;/a&gt; transition to its most recent hosting platform.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That, &amp;amp; they were always supposed to be blog posts anyway&amp;hellip; I didn&amp;rsquo;t have a blog then.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="notice note"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-title"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-sticky-note" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;Note&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="notice-content"&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Jamf Pro API basic authentication method used in this script is deprecated. See the following links for updated auth methods:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://grahamrpugh.com/2024/05/16/jamf-pro-api-authentication.html" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Changes to Classic API authentication in Jamf Pro - what you need to know&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://community.jamf.com/tech-thoughts-180/how-to-convert-classic-api-scripts-to-use-bearer-token-authentication-53426" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;How to convert Classic API scripts to use bearer token authentication&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://trainingcatalog.jamf.com/jamf-pro-api-authentication" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Pro API Authentication Training&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jamf.com/blog/understanding-jamf-pro-api-roles-and-clients/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Understanding Jamf Pro API Roles and Clients&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://learn.jamf.com/en-US/bundle/jamf-pro-documentation-current/page/API_Roles_and_Clients.html" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf API Roles and Clients Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://developer.jamf.com/jamf-pro/docs/jamf-pro-api-overview#authentication-and-authorization" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Jamf Pro API Overview - Authentication and Authorization&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>